Actually, I realize I should think about the coordinate system. The world is 1280x1280. The camera has position (camX, camY) and zoom level. Screen coordinates are derived from world coordinates by:
- screenX = (worldX - camX) * zoom
- screenY = (worldY - camY) * zoom

And inverse:
- worldX = screenX / zoom + camX
- worldY = screenY / zoom + camY

The camera is clamped to world bounds, meaning camX ranges from 0 to 1280 - canvasWidth/zoom, etc.

Mouse coordinates need to be converted from screen to world for clicking on entities.

